e company was formerly known as SCS Transportation, Inc. and changed its name to Saia, Inc. in July 2002. Saia, Inc. was founded in 1924 and is headquartered in Johns Creek, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frederick J. Holzgrefe III | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $235K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Saia, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $8.9B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $27M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 21\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 183% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8318235489736077},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2961747.07},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 23% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Saia EVP Anthony Norwood Withholds 155 Shares at $354.87 and Receives 530 Stock Options","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/saia-evp-ant